	\noindent{Social} behavior in humans are a complex subject that can seem almost impossible to fully understand. A good example of this are usage of sarcasm in interactions, which is famously easily to create misunderstandings, especially when written, because of intonation and voice features are often used to clear markers for a sarcastic comment. Therefore this project aims to explore how well different machine learning models can classify sarcasm from orinary sentences. The models that will be examined are Logistic regression with TF-IDF features, LSTM and BERT. The data that will be used to training, validation and testing will be sarcastic comments taken from two social media platforms. After training and validation, the models preformance was compared and the result was ---. (Some more discussion will be added here too)

